msgid "freeports\\_dev.ci.gate"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate:1 of
msgid ""
"``freeports-dev ci-check``: the one place that decides whether a commit "
"goes through."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate:3 of
msgid ""
"It reads what the measurements left in ``reports/``, the minima in "
"``ci.yaml`` and the class of the branch, prints one table, and chooses an"
" exit status. It measures nothing itself, which is the point: when a "
"commit is refused, the number that refused it is sitting in a file, "
"written by a command the person can re-run by hand. A gate whose figures "
"cannot be reproduced is a gate that gets switched off the first time it "
"is wrong."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate:9 of
msgid ""
"Five verdicts, and the two that are easy to get wrong are the reason this"
" module exists:"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate:12 of
msgid "verdict"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate:12 of
msgid "meaning"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate:12 of
msgid "dev"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate:12 of
msgid "prod"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate:14 of
msgid "``pass``"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate:14 of
msgid "measured, at or above the minimum"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate:14 of
msgid "--"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate:15 of
msgid "``below``"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate:15 of
msgid "measured, under the minimum"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate:15 freeports_dev.ci.gate:16 freeports_dev.ci.gate:17
#: of
msgid "notify"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate:15 of
msgid "refuse"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate:16 of
msgid "``unmeasured``"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate:16 of
msgid "the tool is missing, or the run failed"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate:16 freeports_dev.ci.gate:17 of
msgid "**refuse**"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate:17 of
msgid "``stale``"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate:17 of
msgid "measured at a commit other than HEAD"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate:18 of
msgid "``no threshold``"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate:18 of
msgid "nothing configured for it"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate:18 of
msgid "listed"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate:21 of
msgid ""
"**``unmeasured`` is never a pass.** A figure nobody could compute is not "
"a figure above the threshold, and reporting it as one is exactly the "
"failure this project already ruled out for a methodology page it could "
"not reach: unverifiable is not granted. The message names the missing "
"tool and the command that installs it, because a refusal a person cannot "
"act on is a refusal they will route around."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate:27 of
msgid ""
"**``stale`` is what makes the fast/slow split honest.** The hook measures"
" the fast metrics at every commit and *reads* the slow ones from the last"
" ``make ci``. Without staleness the split would quietly become a way of "
"never measuring the slow half at all: a figure from three weeks ago would"
" gate today's commit and nobody would know. On dev it is a notification; "
"on prod it refuses, and the message says `run make ci`. A prod commit is "
"usually a deliberate merge and paying minutes for it once is the price of"
" the number being true."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate:34 of
msgid ""
"Two of the things gated here are not numbers and have no threshold: the "
"**outcome of a test suite**, which the caller reports with ``--suite "
"name:passed|failed``, and the **fingerprint/version rule**. They are "
"conditions, and they are printed under the metric table rather than "
"inside it."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate:38 of
msgid ""
"What may refuse is a threshold, a suite and the fingerprint rule. **Grant"
" integrity never refuses, on any branch** -- that rule is unchanged and "
"deliberate: a granted reference output regenerated by ``make-tests`` is "
"ordinary work, and a contributor who does not hold the granting key could"
" not clear such a gate at all."
msgstr ""

