#: ../../source/generated/modules/freeports_dev.ci.gate.rst:39:<autosummary>:1
#: freeports_dev.ci.gate.Verdict:1 of
msgid ""
"One metric's line in the table: what was asked, what was found, and what "
"that means."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate.Condition:3 of
msgid ""
"``state`` is what a suite has and a plain yes/no rule does not. A rule "
"either holds or it does not; a suite can also be stale or never have been"
" run here, and those are different things to tell somebody -- one means "
"\"fix the code\", the others mean \"run the command\", and ``command`` "
"carries which command."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate.Condition.fails:1 of
msgid "Whether this line stops a commit on a prod branch."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate.Condition.fails:3 of
msgid ""
"A suite is judged by its state rather than by ``ok`` so that ``stale`` "
"and ``not run`` carry their own weight: they refuse, for the reason "
"``unmeasured`` refuses among the metrics. A plain rule has only the yes "
"and the no."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate.Gate.refuses:1 of
msgid "Whether this commit is stopped."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate.Gate.refuses:3 of
msgid ""
"Only on a prod branch, and only for a threshold, a suite or the "
"fingerprint rule. On dev every one of these is a notification, which is "
"what was asked and is a change from the behaviour the engine's hook had "
"before this work."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate.SUITE_STALE:1 of
msgid "The suite last ran at another commit. Says nothing about this code."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate.UNMEASURED:1 of
msgid "Nobody could compute it. Never a pass."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate.Verdict.fails:1 of
msgid "Whether this line would refuse a commit on a prod branch."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate.evaluate:3 of
#, python-format
msgid ""
"A metric with no minimum is still listed. Being able to see a figure "
"nobody has decided about yet is how a threshold gets seeded at a real "
"number instead of an aspiration -- which is the mistake the pipeline this"
" replaces made, asking 90 % of a figure that read 25.93 %."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate.judge_metric:3 of
msgid ""
"Unmeasured is decided before staleness and both before the comparison, "
"because each answers a question the next one presupposes: there is no "
"point asking whether a figure is current if nobody could compute it, and "
"none asking whether it clears a bar if it describes other code."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate.judge_suite:3 of
msgid ""
"Never run is decided before staleness and both before the outcome, "
"because each answers a question the next presupposes: there is no point "
"asking when a suite ran if it never has, and none asking whether it "
"passed if what passed was other code."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate.parse_suite:3 of
msgid ""
"What is given on the command line describes this moment, so it outranks "
"whatever the same suite left in ``reports/`` at some earlier commit. "
"Anything that is not exactly ``passed`` is a failure, including a "
"spelling nobody intended: a hook writes this string from a shell "
"variable, and the one way this must not fail is by reading an "
"unrecognised word as success."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate.parse_suite:8 of
msgid ""
"A name no registry claims is still honoured rather than dropped. A "
"repository may run a suite this workspace has never heard of, and "
"swallowing it would be the one failure mode that matters -- a suite "
"reported as passing because nobody recognised its name."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.gate.render_text:3 of
msgid ""
"The sentences are the part that matters. A table of verdicts tells "
"somebody a commit was refused; a sentence naming the tool, the figure and"
" the command tells them what to do about it, and only the second kind of "
"message survives contact with a person in a hurry."
msgstr ""

